---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

export async function getStaticPaths({ paginate }) {
    const posts = (await getCollection('blog')).sort(
        (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf()
    );
    return paginate(posts, { pageSize: 10 });
}

const { page } = Astro.props;
const title = "Simon Ganz";
const description = "Personal blog of Simon Ganz, covering topics such as screenwriting, comedy, and technology.";

// Helper to render MDX excerpt
// Astro doesn't have a built-in "render just excerpt" for MDX easily without loading full content.
// But we can check for "<!-- more -->" in the raw body if we want, OR simple render the whole thing and hide with CSS (not ideal).
// Ideally, we render the Content component. If the MDX file has "<!-- more -->" (which we replaced READMORE with),
// MDX itself doesn't automatically split it unless we use a remark plugin.
// HOWEVER, a simpler Astro way for MDX is just to render the content and let the user decide.
// But MDX compiles to a component.
//
// A common Astro pattern is to use a remark plugin to put the excerpt in frontmatter or just render the whole listing if acceptable.
// Given "legacy look and feel", the index page showed:
// 1. Full content IF no readmore.
// 2. Partial content IF readmore.
//
// We can achieve this by rendering the post <Content /> but we need to stop it at the separator if present.
// Since we are using standard "<!-- more -->", we can use `remark-excerpt` or similar, 
// OR we can manually process this.
//
// Let's try rendering the <Content /> and assume we will hide the rest via CSS? No, that sends too much data.
// 
// Better approach: We injected reference to `<!-- more -->` in migration.
// Let's just render the full content for now, but restrict it if needed?
// Actually, Astro's `post.render()` returns `{ Content, headings, remarkPluginFrontmatter }`.
// If we want valid HTML on the index, we really should render the component.
// 
// Let's use a standard trick: render the component components but we need to split.
// Actually, `<!-- more -->` is a comment. In MDX it might be stripped or stay as comment.
//
// Let's assume for this step we will just render the `Content` component.
// AND we will implement a custom component wrapper to handle the "read more" logic?
// No, that's complex.
//
// Simpler: The migration script replaced READMORE with `<!-- more -->`.
// Let's use `remark` to split the content.
// Actually, let's keep it simple. Index page renders a list of posts. 
// We will iterate and render <post.Content />.
// But we need to define components that handle the `more` tag?
//
// Wait, the user said: "The way the old site worked... by default the whole blog post was on the index page unless... READMORE".
// So we DO want to render the full content by default.
// 
// So, we will render <Content /> for each post in the loop.
// BUT, if there IS a more tag, we only want to show the first part.
// 
// Astro doesn't support "rendering part of MDX" out of the box easily without plugins.
// PROPOSAL: Use a remark plugin to truncate the AST at the `more` marker.
// I will invoke the `Content` component, but I'll configure mdx with a remark plugin in `astro.config.mjs`?
// No, that would apply to the individual post page too!
//
// Solution: We need TWO renderings? No.
// Solution: The migration replaced READMORE with `<!-- more -->`.
// I will create a `Preview.astro` component that takes the post.
// It will render the content.
// BUT, how to truncate?
// 
// Let's update `astro.config.mjs` to include a remark plugin that populates `excerpt`?
// Or we can just do what the user asked: "Plan a way to replace this functionality".
//
// I'll stick to the plan:
// 1. Use a remark plugin to extract excerpt to frontmatter?
// 2. OR, simply string manipulate the compiled output? No, compiled is code.
//
// Let's go with: Render FULL content on index.
// But if "readMoreText" exists in data, we use that?
// No, the marker determines the split point.
//
// Let's add a remark plugin that splits the content if `<!-- more -->` is found, 
// keeping only the first part for a special "excerpt" property? 
// 
// actually, a simpler way for MDX:
// Content on index page:
// <Content components={{ ... }} />
//
// If I use a property in the frontmatter `hasReadMore: true`, I can decide to render differently.
//
// Let's try to just render everything for now (simplest "modern" Astro).
// BUT, if the file is huge, that's bad.
//
// Let's stick to the user's specific request.
// "Plan a way to replace this functionality".
//
// I will implement a custom `PostContent.astro` that renders the post.
// And on the index page, I will use a remark plugin to ADD `excerpt` HTML to the frontmatter (injected).
// Then on index, I render `post.render().remarkPluginFrontmatter.excerpt` if it exists.
// If NOT, I render `<Content />`.
// 
// Let's do that. I need to install `remark-excerpt`? Or write a simple one.
//
// Actually, I can write a local plugin in `remark-excerpt.mjs`.
// And add it to `astro.config.mjs`.
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
    {page.data.map(async (post, index) => {
        const { Content, remarkPluginFrontmatter } = await post.render();
        const hasExcerpt = !!remarkPluginFrontmatter.excerpt;
        const isLast = index === page.data.length - 1;
        
        return (
            <article>
                <header>
                    <h1>
                        <a href={`/${post.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 4)}/${post.data.date.toISOString().slice(5, 7)}/${post.slug}/`} title={post.data.title}>{post.data.title}</a>
                    </h1>
                    <div class='postDate'>
                        <a href={`/${post.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 4)}/${post.data.date.toISOString().slice(5, 7)}/${post.slug}/`} title='Permalink'>
                            <small>
                                {post.data.date.toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
                                    year: 'numeric',
                                    month: 'short',
                                    day: 'numeric',
                                })}
                            </small>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </header>
                
                {hasExcerpt ? (
                    <div set:html={remarkPluginFrontmatter.excerpt} />
                ) : (
                    <Content />
                )}
                
                {hasExcerpt && (
                   <p><a href={`/${post.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 4)}/${post.data.date.toISOString().slice(5, 7)}/${post.slug}/`}>
                        {post.data.readMoreText || "Read more..."}
                   </a></p>
                )}
                
                {!isLast && <hr class='postDivider'>}
            </article>
        );
    })}
    
    <div class="pagination-wrapper">
        <div class="pagination-controls">
            {page.url.prev && <a href={page.url.prev}>Newer Posts</a>}
            {page.url.prev && page.url.next && <span class="separator">•</span>}
            {page.url.next && <a href={page.url.next}>Older Posts</a>}
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .pagination-wrapper {
        text-align: center;
        margin-top: 2em; /* Increased spacing as requested */
        margin-bottom: 3em;
        padding-top: 2em;
        border-top: 3px solid rgb(37,37,37); /* Darker color for visibility */
        width: 100%;
        display: block;
    }
    
    .pagination-controls {
        display: inline-block;
        font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;
        font-size: 18px;
    }
    
    .pagination-controls a {
        color: #999;
        font-weight: 300;
        text-decoration: none;
        margin: 0 10px;
    }

    .pagination-controls a:hover {
        color: #ff3333;
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
    
    .separator {
        color: #ccc;
    }
</style>
